{# The ONBOARDING chrome — `gate`'s sibling, and the third chrome after `shell`
   and that one. A gate is a card offering the one thing a page is for;
   onboarding is a short conversation, so the same centred column carries the
   step's words above the form rather than beside it.

   ONE COLUMN, NOT TWO. A two-column frame was built first and rejected on
   sight: it reads as two subjects where there is one, and it halved the
   form's measure for no gain — a wizard step is a single line of thought, and
   the widest thing in it is the form.

   IT CARRIES THE STEP'S COPY AS PROPS, filled by the wizard form rather than
   by the Island Profile. The copy belongs to the step, and a profile's layout
   settings are static config that cannot differ between step 1 and step 2.

   THE ID IS THE HTMX FRAGMENT BOUNDARY'S ANCHOR: the form swaps its own
   `outerHTML` and this element rides inside it, so copy and fields can never
   describe different steps.

   NOT A SCROLL CONTAINER, for `gate`'s reason: `min-h-screen` with centred
   items lets a long card grow the page instead of clipping itself. #}
<div{{ (attributes ?: create_attribute()).setAttribute('id', 'bakers-onboarding').addClass(['min-h-screen', 'flex', 'items-center', 'justify-center', 'p-gutter', 'bg-app', 'text-text']) }}>
  <div class="w-full max-w-xl min-w-0 flex flex-col items-center gap-group">
    <div class="w-full flex flex-col items-center text-center gap-inline">
      {% if mark %}
        <div>{% block mark %}{{ mark }}{% endblock %}</div>
      {% endif %}
      {% if title %}
        <h1 class="text-section-title" tabindex="-1" x-init="$el.focus({preventScroll: true})">{{ title }}</h1>
      {% endif %}
      {% if description %}
        <p class="text-meta text-text-faint max-w-xs">{{ description }}</p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
    <div class="w-full min-w-0 flex flex-col gap-group p-gutter bg-surface border border-border-2 rounded-md">{% block content %}{% if content %}{{ content }}{% endif %}{% endblock %}</div>
  </div>
</div>
